        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: alcanzar",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "alcanzar — \"to reach, to catch up with\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Después de tres horas alcanzamos al grupo. After three hours we caught up with the group."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It takes c before e: alcancé. Alcanzar un objetivo — to achieve a goal."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "alcanzar is usually traced to spoken Latin incalciāre 'to follow at the heels' (EtymDB), built on calx 'heel'. To catch up is to be on someone's heels."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
